  message: <<EOM
To run Legion, as root:

  sysrc -f /boot/loader.conf kern.racct.enable=1   # rctl limits; reboot once
  zfs create -o mountpoint=/zroot/legion zroot/legion
  sysrc legion_enable=YES legion_args="--zfs-root zroot/legion"
  service legion start
  legion init          # on the first manager; other nodes run legion join

Legion needs pf enabled, with /etc/pf.conf calling its anchors.

  legion doctor --fix pf

shows the lines it would add, asks, checks the new file with pfctl -nf,
keeps the old one as /etc/pf.conf.legion-<time>, then enables and loads pf.
legion init and legion join offer it too. legion doctor checks the rest of
what a host needs and changes nothing.

The daemon logs to /var/log/legion.log. "service legion stop" leaves the
pods running; the next start takes them over.
EOM
